FINDING THE OFFSET TO OVERWRITE THE FUNCTION POINTER

because memcpy() copies 1024 bytes into a 16-byte stack buffer, the overwrite can extend beyond local_buffer and corrupt adjacent stack data.
so when handle_post_request() returns, execution flow may jump to an attacker-controlled address instead of the legitimate caller.


| higher addresses |
-------------------
| return address   |  <-- target
| saved RBP        |
| local_buffer[16] |
-------------------
| lower addresses  |


